    ## Manual Verification Instructions

    Access **http://localhost:8081** with `admin`/`admin`:

    ### 1. View Live Dashboard
    - Navigate to **Dashboard** (home page)
    - ✅ Verify 4 device cards displayed in grid
    - ✅ Each card shows device name, current value, unit, status tag
    - ✅ Gauge charts visible with color zones
    - ✅ Trend line charts showing recent data

    ### 2. Watch Real-time Updates
    - Keep dashboard open
    - Watch gauge needles and values update every ~2 seconds
    - ✅ Verify values change automatically (no page refresh)
    - ✅ Timestamps update in real-time

    ### 3. Check Threshold Indicators
    - Tank Temperature (threshold: warning 28, critical 29)
    - Values are ~27-28°C, may trigger warning
    - ✅ Status tag turns **yellow** (warning) when value ≥ 28
    - ✅ Status tag turns **red** (critical) when value ≥ 29
    - ✅ Status tag is **green** (success) when normal

    ### 4. Verify Gauge Threshold Zones
    - Look at any gauge chart
    - ✅ Green zone: 0 to warning threshold
    - ✅ Yellow zone: warning to critical threshold
    - ✅ Red zone: critical to max
    - ✅ Needle position matches current value

    ### 5. Check Trend Charts
    - Scroll down on each card
    - ✅ Mini line chart shows last 20 readings
    - ✅ X-axis shows timestamps
    - ✅ Hover over chart points to see exact values

    ### 6. Verify WebSocket Connection
    - Open browser DevTools → Network tab → WS filter
    - ✅ See connection to `ws://localhost:8081/ws/live`
    - ✅ Status: 101 Switching Protocols
    - ✅ Messages flowing every 2 seconds

    ### 7. Test Auto-Reconnect
    - In DevTools, close the WebSocket connection manually
    - ✅ Verify console shows "WebSocket disconnected, reconnecting in 5s..."
    - ✅ Connection automatically re-establishes
    - ✅ Dashboard continues updating

    ### 8. Refresh Page
    - Refresh browser (F5)
    - ✅ Dashboard reloads
    - ✅ WebSocket reconnects
    - ✅ Live data resumes immediately

    **All Iteration 4 requirements fulfilled!** ✅ Real-time monitoring dashboard is working with live 4-device demo.
